     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Take a look at JavaScript events in shiny: <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/js-events.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/js-events.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792392081658000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lIZxSGGOvZSYiWCwH_FVh\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/js-events.html</a><div><br></div><div>Specifically, you want the &quot;shiny:connected&quot; event.</div><div><br></div><div>What&#39;s happening is that the code does run when the document is ready, but that only means that the HTML finished rendering and shiny isn&#39;t ready yet. The fix in your case: replace `$(document).ready(function() { ` with `$(document).on(&quot;shiny:connected&quot;, function() { `</div></div>"
    ],
